# The transpiler rewrite's strict xfail list (TESTING.md, "Golden gate").
#
#   <input-set>/<relpath> <target> <reason>
#
# <target> is a dialect name, or `parse` (the output file's stem under the
# input's golden directory). The `ir` and `report` lines went with the IR
# (phase 6): `golden diff` passes over a baseline's `ir.json` and
# `report.json`. `golden diff --xfail` fails on
# any difference not listed here, and on a listed line that is now identical
# (XPASS): delete the line then. Every line is a reviewed, intended change.

# Phase 2 (syntax::ast_to_ir): today's spice.peg `Str <- '"' (!'"' .)* '"'`
# reads across a logical line's end, so a stray `"` in one card swallows the
# next card into one raw line ("v2\" 2 0 1\nv3 3\" 0 1"); the tokenizer ends
# a string at its line (Xyce RG §2.1.39), so the two cards stay two. A bug
# of the old card grammar, not reproduced: phase 7 keeps the new reading.
xyce/INVALID_CHARS/double_quote_fails_device_name.cir cdl the IR above differs (one more raw card), so the xschem layout lists it
xyce/INVALID_CHARS/double_quote_fails_device_name.cir verilog the IR above differs (one more raw card), so the xschem layout lists it
xyce/INVALID_CHARS/double_quote_fails_node_name.cir cdl the IR above differs (one more raw card), so the xschem layout lists it
xyce/INVALID_CHARS/double_quote_fails_node_name.cir verilog the IR above differs (one more raw card), so the xschem layout lists it
xyce/INVALID_CHARS/double_quote_fails_node_name.cir espice the refusal quotes the first raw line, which is now one card
xyce/INVALID_CHARS/double_quote_fails_node_name.cir hspice the refusal quotes the first raw line, which is now one card
xyce/INVALID_CHARS/double_quote_fails_node_name.cir ltspice the refusal quotes the first raw line, which is now one card
xyce/INVALID_CHARS/double_quote_fails_node_name.cir ngspice the refusal quotes the first raw line, which is now one card
xyce/INVALID_CHARS/double_quote_fails_node_name.cir spectre the refusal quotes the first raw line, which is now one card
xyce/INVALID_CHARS/double_quote_fails_node_name.cir vacask the refusal quotes the first raw line, which is now one card

# Phase 3 behaviour (syntax::resolve; golden reads each kit file in its
